  // Your own weather schedule. vMenu only reads this file when
  // vMenu.Enhanced.WeatherOptions.WeatherCycle is set to "custom" and weather sync is turned on.
  //
  // The schedule is a list of blocks played from top to bottom. Each block says how many in-game
  // hours a weather lasts. When the last block ends, the list starts over from the top. One in-game
  // hour is two real minutes at normal speed, so 24 hours here is one full in-game day.
  //
  // "hours" is how long the block lasts, any number above 0 (1.5 works too).
  // "weather" is one of: CLEAR, EXTRASUNNY, CLOUDS, OVERCAST, RAIN, CLEARING, THUNDER, SMOG, FOGGY,
  //   XMAS, SNOW, SNOWLIGHT, BLIZZARD, HALLOWEEN, NEUTRAL, RAIN_HALLOWEEN, SNOW_HALLOWEEN.
  // "blackout" is optional. "city" turns the city lights off, "all" turns the city and vehicle
  //   lights off. Leave it out to keep the lights on. This only happens while the blackout option
  //   in the menu is on "Follow Weather Schedule".
  //
  // "snowPass" keeps snow on the ground for the whole schedule while the snow option in the menu is
  // on automatic, and makes the temperatures wintery, just like the built in snowy schedule.
  //
  // A block with a typo is skipped and the server console says which one. If nothing usable is
  // left, the default GTA Online schedule is used instead.
  //
  // The schedule below is the GTA Online one, with a few rainy and stormy nights added. The comment
  // behind each block is the in-game day and time it starts. The schedule always starts at midnight,
  // so these times stay right as long as all hours together add up to whole days (a multiple of 24)
  // and nobody has moved or frozen the in-game clock. This one is 384 hours, which is 16 days.

